WEBVTT

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.080
<b>Fan</b>

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.830
Fan!

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.500
Good morning. You're here early, Nishikata.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.460
G'morning. Same to you, Takagi-san.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.830
I figured it was going to be extra hot today.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.790
So I left before the sun was all the way out.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:49.790
Oh yeah?

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.540
It was so hot in my room that I woke up.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.710
What's the deal? It's almost October.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.170
It sure is hot.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.830
I've got just the thing.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.540
Now that looks handy!

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.250
Ah! So nice and cool!

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.750
Man, I'm so glad I brought this.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.790
How's it feel, Takagi-san? Bet you're jealous!

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.290
Weep over your lack of a fan while
watching me enjoy a refreshing breeze!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.080
Hey, use it on me too.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.630
Why should I?!

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.790
Because I feel hot.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.960
Well, join the club.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:39.790
Okay.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.420
Then let's make a game of it.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:42.880
A game?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:43.880
Yeah!

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.330
If I win, you fan me.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.170
All right. But what if I win?

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.040
Then I'll fan you instead.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.880
This is paradise!

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.380
I could go for that.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:01.790
Deal.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:02.880
Great!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.500
Let's see here...

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.670
This'll do.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.250
An eraser?

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:14.580
Whoever can use the fan to move
this eraser farther is the winner.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.330
Sounds good.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.750
Okay. Then you go first.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.170
So, all I gotta do is move it more than her?

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.210
That mean this is a battle of power and stamina.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.670
I have the advantage!

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:39.960
Here goes!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.040
Move!

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.790
Move! Move! Move! Move!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.630
MOOOOVE!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.040
It's working!

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.750
Did you see that? Stupid Takagi-san!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.460
That feels good.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.130
Were you watching?! The eraser moved!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.790
Yeah. I saw it.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.500
It moved just a tiny bit, huh?

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.130
I didn't think it would budge. I'm shocked!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:14.750
I see how it is.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:21.040
She thought I couldn't move the eraser, so she made up
this "game" just to get me to cool her down!

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.500
Well, I guess it's your turn now.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.630
Done.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:40.670
Huh?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.960
I moved it farther than you.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.040
Wha?

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.880
You realize, all I said was to "use the fan
to move the eraser farther", right?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.630
Okay. Time for you to fan me.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.380
Fudge. How could this have happened?

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.210
Everything was supposed to go my way!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.040
Curses!

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.460
If I stand here, you get some of the breeze too, right?

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.130
Come on, get to fanning.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.750
Uh, right.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.460
Looks like the heat is getting to you.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.250
Fanning you is hard work.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.960
Plus, I put a lot of effort into moving that eraser.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.380
Oh?

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:01.960
What's your problem?!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.000
I think I'll feel even cooler if I move closer to you.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.420
You stopped again.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.210
Gosh, it's so hot.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:21.130
Something must be wrong with the weather.
That's gotta be it.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.040
Hot...

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:24.830
So hot...

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:29.210
<b>Bewilder Ball</b>

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:27.920
Bewilder Ball!

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.130
Seriously! The main character is so freaking cool!

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.960
He throws a ball that's like a special attack!

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.540
It's basically a battle manga, guys!

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.580
The coach is strict but loves baseball more than anyone!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.250
The manager is an ex-player
who got injured unexpectedly!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:46.210
Plus, the rival team is insanely strong!

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.290
I'm telling you, you gotta read it!

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.710
<b>Summer Slammer</b>

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.710
Man, I love this series.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.500
Aw yeah! This technique is just so sick!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.880
Whoa! I recognize that pose!

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.790
Is he really going to do it?!

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.290
The ultimate pitch!

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.920
Yes! He calls it...

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.080
Bewilder Ball! Time Lea-!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.380
Hey there, looks like you were doing something cool.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:52.580
Crap! I totally let my guard down!

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:55.080
<b>Summer Slammer</b>

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:57.830
She must've overheard me talking yesterday, and
then rolled that ping pong ball toward me on purpose!

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.580
Just how calculating can she be? Darn you, Takagi-san!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.920
Um... so, about this...

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.000
Could you please keep it between us?

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.960
Gosh, I dunno.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:25.080
You looked like you were having so much fun.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.130
I kind of want to try it now.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.790
I'll agree to keep my mouth shut if you can strike me out.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:35.630
Fine.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.960
Okay! Play ball!

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.540
I absolutely HAVE to win!

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.750
Oh hey! Do your impression of that manga again!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.040
Like you were doing earlier.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.130
N-no way!

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:58.540
That being said, I'm going to need my imagination
if I want to boost my focus!

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:03.000
Well folks, we're down to the last batter.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.170
Nishikata is now on the verge
of fulfilling his dream of victory!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:10.210
But stepping up to the plate is
his long-time rival, Takagi-san!

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:14.920
And throughout their history of matches,
Takagi-san has won them all!

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.880
Two and three.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.290
Nishikata, play it safe and throw a ball for starters.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:22.960
What?!

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.540
I'll do it for them!

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.790
For Coach Tanabe, who's only strict
out of his love for baseball.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.460
<b>It's all on you,</b>

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.460
<b>Nishikata</b>

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:35.210
For Takao, whose injury led him
to becoming our manager.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.540
If only I hadn't gotten that injury!

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.170
And also...

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.290
Go team! Go team!

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:41.040
Just play it cool!

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.000
We've got your back, bro!

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.290
For all the people who supported me along the way.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.420
This will be a pitch filled with gratitude!

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.710
BEWILDER BALL! TIME LEAAAAAP!

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.330
Strike!

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:03.130
I'm just getting started.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:06.750
Is that one of the lines from that manga?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:08.710
I let it slip...

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.170
Come on! Throw your next pitch!

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.880
Darn it! The illusion is totally shattered!

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.830
I can't believe I just screwed it all up...

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.670
Come on, I'm waiting.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.290
Whatever. I'll just have to power through!

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.790
Time Leap! Bewil- AH!

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:31.290
That's wrong! I got it backwards!

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:38.880
WHAMO!

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:47.290
Home Run!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.830
Looks like I win.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.750
Is that another manga thing?

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.960
No... it's a me thing.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:08.000
Um... Takagi-san...

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:12.710
Please don't tell anyone...
what I was doing in here alone...

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.330
Well, I dunno.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.170
I guess I could.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.710
But in exchange...

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.250
I want you to lend me that baseball manga!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.750
Wait, are you sure that's all?

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:31.750
Yeah!

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.670
I'm not sure you'll find it very interesting, though...

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:37.920
That's okay.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:42.670
Because I want to know everything
I can about the things you like!

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:50.330
<b>Summer Slammer</b>

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.330
After I finish reading it,

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:50.330
let's do what we just did and have another showdown
while pretending to be the characters.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:54.210
F-fine, but just so you know, I wasn't pretending!

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:05.790
It's almost the time of year
we change to our winter uniforms,

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.170
but it hasn't shown any signs of getting cooler yet...

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:10.040
The cicadas are still loud as heck, too.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:12.960
What is it?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:13.540
A cat!

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.750
<b>Cat Rescue</b>

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:18.000
Cat Rescue.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.250
Come on out!

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:23.210
You sure do love cats.

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.500
Which is weird since you own a dog.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:30.040
Come here, plumpy!

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:34.790
Don't be scared now! This way!

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:36.500
Huh?

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.880
She doesn't seem interested. Let's go.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:39.920
Lame...

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.710
Cats are just the cutest, aren't they?

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:47.500
You know, I think this cat is stuck in there.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:47.670
I guess.

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:48.500
What?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.500
Although, I could be wrong.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:56.710
You're right. It looks like she's struggling to move.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.790
That's gotta be it!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.040
Just look at the distress in her eyes!

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.750
Darn it. Just hang on, kitty! I'm gonna get you out!

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.250
Ugh, I can't reach...

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.330
Fine then.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.040
Outta the way. I'll handle this.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.920
Your arms might be long enough to reach her!

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.290
This way, girl.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:21.670
She just went farther back...

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.630
Because your face is too scary?

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:25.710
Keep your comments to yourself.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.790
You can do it, Yukari-chan!

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:29.920
Did you get her?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.790
No, I didn't. But now I'm stuck in here and can't move.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:35.670
Uh oh!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.880
Hang tight! We've got you!

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.420
Ouch! Stop!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.750
You gotta pull me more gently!

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.210
Can you at least move your head a little?

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:47.710
Yeah, I think so...

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:52.580
Jeez, this is what we get for counting
our chickens before they hatch.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.920
You're getting the meaning of that wrong.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.500
Huh? Then what idiom fits here?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.830
Even Homer sometimes nods.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.750
Don't call me Homer!

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.880
This is more of a "going for wool and coming home..."

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.290
Oh, I got unstuck.

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.710
Thank heavens!

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.420
Yeah, seriously.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.540
It's raining.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.630
That explains why the cicadas got quiet.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.880
Let's go somewhere we can get out of the rain!

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:19.790
That way.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.040
Looks like it's not stopping soon.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.540
We didn't bring any umbrellas. This sucks.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.920
I hope that cat from earlier is okay...

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:41.210
That cat... just came out of the gap we saw, yeah?

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.170
Yeah.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:50.460
I guess she wasn't plumpy, she was just fluffy!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.750
So, she wasn't stuck after all.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.420
Whew! That's a relief!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.710
Come here, girl!

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.170
I was gonna snatch her up and give her all the pets...

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:10.040
Sometimes things don't go how you want them to.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:21.580
More rain today.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:24.290
Ugh.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:25.670
Seriously?

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.880
Not again! I didn't get my coat before I left!

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.460
Yeah, it really gets my goat, too.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.080
That's not what she said.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.130
Rain?!

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:40.880
Oh dear.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.460
The forecast said it could go either way.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.420
Y-yeah, it did.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.460
Crap! I didn't bring an umbrella!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.670
That means I'll be soaking wet when I get home...

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.670
Wait! I still have my last resort.

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:01.000
Oh, there's the bell. Be careful on your way home.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.080
Yes, sir.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.420
<b>OFFICE</b>

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:18.130
<b>Lost and Found</b>

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.330
Excuse me!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.130
Are there any umbrellas in the lost and found?!

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:18.630
Yeah, just one.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:20.170
Please let me borrow it!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:21.790
Sure.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.040
Write your name and year down here.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:28.210
<b>Record</b>

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:27.830
Okay!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.920
Awesome! They had one!

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:34.460
The pink makes it a little embarrassing, though.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.670
If she had found out I didn't bring my own...

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.670
Really? Wanna get cozy under mine?

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.670
Oh? Guess you're too shy!

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.380
That would've sucked!

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.670
Dude, share your umbrella with me.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.630
Sure thing. But you gotta help me with my math.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:03.540
I wonder if Takagi-san went home already...

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:08.040
Thinking about it, I just left without saying goodbye.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:17.790
There's a good reason I have to hurry home today.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.170
Because very soon...

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:28.080
<b>Summer Slammer</b>

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:28.080
<b>Dyna Soccer</b>

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:27.380
The collaboration TV special between Dynamite Super
Soccer and Summer Slammer will start airing!

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:34.380
The heroes of soccer and baseball are going to face-off
in a game of kickball! It's gonna be so intense!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.630
As a fan, I absolutely cannot miss it!

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:41.920
But, man, I screwed up.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:46.130
Next time the forecast is iffy,
I'm definitely bringing an umbrella.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.250
I'm super lucky to have gotten the last one at school.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:54.920
I wonder...

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:00.040
Did Takagi-san bring an umbrella today?

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:10.330
Well, I mean, it's Takagi-san. She must have.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:11.960
No worries.

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:24.670
But that one time... she actually did forget.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.670
And maybe today is the same...

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:39.330
No way! She obviously must have remembered today!

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.880
It's Takagi-san, after all!

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:45.630
I gotta hurry home and check out
the Dyna Soccer vs. Summer Slammer special!

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:48.290
Right! Come on! Let's go!

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:06.000
I hope the rain lets up.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:22.630
Nishikata?

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:27.580
Did you forget your umbrella? Just curious.

00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:29.880
Yeah. I did.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:31.960
Well, shucks.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.790
So, hey...

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.380
Uh, s-so...

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.330
you're doing homework?

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.330
Yeah.

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.420
I thought the rain might let up if I waited,
so I'm killing time.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:59.000
O-oh.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:02.330
What about you? Were you able to borrow one?

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:03.420
Huh?

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:06.000
You sprinted out of here after homeroom ended,

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:09.080
because you wanted to borrow an umbrella
from the lost and found, right?

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:10.790
She knows.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.460
Well, I got lucky and there was one left.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:15.830
Oh yeah?

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:19.330
So, like...

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:22.210
Would you...

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:27.920
...like to go together?

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.330
Yeah!

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:37.040
I'm so happy.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.420
You actually invited me to get cozy under your umbrella!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.290
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:46.920
Sorry, kidding.

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:49.210
I know I shouldn't tease you.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:52.380
Seeing as how you were kind
enough to come back for me.

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.170
I noticed your shoulder is a little wet.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:59.710
That means you came back out of concern, right?

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:04.000
Well... yeah.

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:08.460
Even though your favorite TV special airs today.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:10.290
How do you know that?!

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.580
That's easy. Because I know everything about you.

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:38.750
You know, next time it rains I just
might forget my umbrella on purpose.

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:39.920
Huh?

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.710
If I do, will you invite me to share yours again?

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.460
S-sure, whatever.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.080
Oh really?

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:54.000
So you wanna get cozy under the umbrella that badly?

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:57.920
You just said that you weren't gonna tease me!

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.250
Oh, sorry. I couldn't help myself.

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:02.830
You better bring your umbrella, darn it!

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:04.580
Ugh!

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.290
<b>Rain</b>
